  "content": "# Implementing a Bounded LRU Cache in Python\n\n## Overview\n\nA **Least Recently Used (LRU) cache** is a data structure that evicts the least recently accessed item when its capacity is exceeded. It is widely used in databases, web servers, and operating systems to improve performance by keeping frequently accessed data in fast memory.\n\nPython's `collections.OrderedDict` provides an ideal foundation for an LRU cache because it maintains insertion order and supports efficient `move_to_end()` operations, giving us O(1) average-case complexity for both `get` and `put`.\n\n---\n\n## The Complete Implementation\n\n",
